<title>LEBANON: Lebanon's Banque Audi half-year profit $9.1 mln.</title>
<headline>Lebanon's Banque Audi half-year profit $9.1 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's Banque Audi reported profits of 14.336 billion Lebanese pounds ($9.125 million) in the first half of 1996 compared with 20.1 billion pounds ($12.6 million) in the whole of 1995.</p>
<p>An unaudited consolidated income statement for Banque Audi and its subsidiary Infibank at June 30 gave the following results (In millions of Lebanese pounds. Comparative figures for 30/6/95 were not issued):</p>
<p>    Total interest received	    154,925</p>
<p>    Total interest paid		  115,733</p>
<p>    Bad debts and provisions	     3,260</p>
<p>Net interest margin after</p>
<p>    provision for bad debts	     35,932</p>
<p>    Net financial income		  43,295</p>
<p>    Net profit before tax		 15,805</p>
<p>    Income tax				 1,469</p>
<p>    Net profit after tax		  14,336</p>
<p>The consolidated balance sheet at June 30, 1996, showed that assets rose 10.5 percent over the end of 1995 (millions of Lebanese pounds at end of period):</p>
<p>						  30/6/96	  31/12/95</p>
<p>    Total assets			   2,338,871	2,115,959</p>
<p>    Lebanese t-bills			 787,925	  824,920</p>
<p>    Loans to customers		     669,348	  589,261</p>
<p>    Short term loans			 616,456	  530,831</p>
<p>    Deposits from customers	    2,069,380	1,869,197</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity		   150,691	  137,237</p>
<p>($1 = 1,596 Lebanese pounds at 31/12/95)</p>
<p>($1 = 1,571 Lebanese pounds at 30/6/96)</p>
</text>
